Andy Johnson wrote:

> If I'm not mistaken, the Linux version of nethack'll run on any Linux 
> terminal; it's not special for a particular flavor. Someone correct me 
> if I'm wrong.

You're wrong :)

The i386 binary will work on all "PCs"; however it will not work on sparc,
hppa, alpha, powerpc, etc., which is why any Linux distribution that caters
to these platforms will have separate binaries for each.  Look, for
example, in:

ftp://ftp.debian.org/debian/dists/sarge/main/

or more specifically:

ftp://ftp.debian.org/debian/pool/main/n/nethack/

Linux is not a "virtual machine" like java, for instance, uses.

